{"title":"Find Kth Bit In Nth Binary String","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Given two positive integers n and k, the binary string Sn is formed as follows:\n\nS1 = \"0\"\nSi = Si - 1 + \"1\" + reverse(invert(Si - 1)) for i > 1\n\nWhere + denotes the concatenation operation, reverse(x) returns the reversed string x, and invert(x) inverts all the bits in x (0 changes to 1 and 1 changes to 0).\nFor example, the first four strings in the above sequence are:\n\nS1 = \"0\"\nS2 = \"011\"\nS3 = \"0111001\"\nS4 = \"011100110110001\"\n\nReturn the kth bit in Sn. It is guaranteed that k is valid for the given n.\n\nReturn the one-character string at the 1-based position k in the recursively defined string S_n.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: n = 3, k = 1\nOutput: \"0\"\n```\n\nExplanation: S3 is \"0111001\".\nThe 1st bit is \"0\".\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: n = 4, k = 11\nOutput: \"1\"\n```\n\nExplanation: S4 is \"011100110110001\".\nThe 11th bit is \"1\".\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 ≤ n ≤ 20\n- 1 ≤ k ≤ 2^n - 1\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def findKthBit(self, n: int, k: int) -> str:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().findKthBit","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"},{"name":"k","type":"int"}],"returnType":"str","tests":[{"input":[1,1],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,1019],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,118],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,13],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,147],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,161],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,189],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,227],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,287],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,290],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,292],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,304],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,320],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,331],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,359],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,363],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,394],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,398],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,460],"expected":"0"},{"input":[10,544],"expected":"1"},{"input":[10,559],"expected":"1"},{"input":[1